1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Nightingale is a shared care workspace that keeps
longitudinal records, review decisions, and audience boundaries on one patient page.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:16,500
This recording uses synthetic data, a hosted HTTPS workspace,
and a deliberate separation between sources, suggestions, and publication.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:25,000
A ranked item is a workflow aid, not a diagnosis,
and it never silently replaces a human-authored record.

4
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:32,000
I will move from Staff to Clinician to Patient,
with role changes outside the camera frame.

5
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:43,000
I start with Glance View, where content, status, next action,
risk context, and priority appear together.

6
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:54,000
The screen is deliberately capped at six items,
keeping the first clinical read compact instead of overwhelming.

7
00:00:54,500 --> 00:01:04,000
The protected allergy conflict appears first even when
ordinary candidates carry a higher numerical priority.

8
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:15,000
Protected attention is a separate selection policy; it does not
turn a workflow number into a medical risk score.

9
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:26,000
The explanation makes the ranking auditable: protected candidates first,
then deterministic priority, time, and resource ordering.

10
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:37,000
I open the conflict to inspect two contradictory assertions
without editing or resolving either source.

11
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:49,000
The reported allergy and the denied allergy remain separate,
with their own authors, timestamps, and verification states.

12
00:01:49,500 --> 00:02:00,000
Each assertion links to an immutable source version and an exact
highlighted span, rather than a copied approximation.

13
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:12,000
The source panel keeps the originating version distinct from the record's
current version, so later edits remain explainable.

14
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:21,500
Staff can inspect both sources, but the clinical decision controls
stay unavailable in this role.

15
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:31,500
Comments and Tasks are collaboration entry points; opening a drawer
does not change clinical truth or create a task.

16
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:41,500
I now switch to Clinician outside the camera, then return
to the same synthetic patient workspace.

17
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Clinician review exposes adjudication, version history, and conflict
choices that Staff cannot submit.

18
00:02:51,500 --> 00:03:00,500
A stale same-section write returns a deterministic conflict instead
of silently overwriting the newer version.

19
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:10,500
The audit preserves both submissions, so a reviewer can see what happened
and which version was current.

20
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:20,000
History shows an earlier version beside the current record,
without requiring a fixed version number.

21
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:30,000
Compare makes the Before and After text explicit,
while the original timeline entry remains available.

22
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:40,000
A revert creates a new version; it never erases previous snapshots,
audit metadata, or source provenance.

23
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:50,500
From a timeline entry, Prepare patient update opens an explicit
patient-publication review rather than changing visibility.

24
00:03:51,000 --> 00:04:01,000
The workflow begins in Draft and shows the immutable source evidence
behind the proposed patient-facing content.

25
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:12,000
Accepting an internal AI suggestion does not publish it to the patient;
those are separate user actions.

26
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:22,000
Dosage checks are visible before approval, and unsupported or mismatched
dosage remains fail-closed.

27
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:32,000
Clinician approval and explicit Publish are distinct gates; this prototype
does not claim external message delivery.

28
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:42,500
The Voice panel uses a prerecorded synthetic care conversation
and a prepared timestamped transcript.

29
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:53,000
It demonstrates a reviewable source path, not live ASR, diarization,
speaker attribution, or microphone capture.

30
00:04:53,500 --> 00:05:03,500
If a provider fails, the system surfaces an explicit failure state
and keeps existing records available.

31
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:13,000
The failure path is evidence-backed; the prototype does not silently
fabricate a successful fixture result.

32
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:23,000
I switch to Patient outside the camera and show only
the audience-specific shared care projection.

33
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:33,000
The patient view contains current care information and its safe Voice fixture,
without internal review controls.

34
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:43,500
Glance, comments, tasks, conflict details, raw AI output, and source
workflow identifiers stay outside the Patient projection.

35
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:53,000
Publication is therefore a gate before sharing, not an automatic
consequence of accepting an internal suggestion.

36
00:05:53,500 --> 00:06:03,500
The remaining gaps are stated as evidence boundaries,
not hidden claims about a general clinical system.

37
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Phone-only onboarding, multilingual ASR, external delivery receipts,
and broad medication interpretation are not implemented here.

38
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:24,000
The prototype deliberately abstains when its bounded rules lack support,
instead of inventing clinical certainty.

39
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:34,000
These limits are deliberate scope decisions and point to the next build
step rather than a false finish.

40
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:44,000
The repository includes the required application tests for RBAC,
revisions, provenance, and concurrent edits.

41
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:54,000
The local closure run recorded 194 backend tests and 86.62 percent
global application coverage.

42
00:06:54,500 --> 00:07:04,000
PostgreSQL 18 CI passed, and the existing Render service is live
on the exact runtime candidate.

43
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:12,000
The hosted authenticated benchmark remains a disclosed supplementary gap,
not a claim we are hiding.

44
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:22,000
The next step is final human recording, full video QA, and submission
packaging after the video exists.
